       ("Charlotte&rsquo;s social split", "<p>Charlotte has two social personalities sharing one skyline. Uptown is polish: banks, headquarters, game-day suits. South End and NoDa are the opposite energy: breweries, galleries, food halls and a creative scene that punishes anything that smells corporate. Add Panthers and Hornets fandom, a NASCAR heritage, and neighborhoods that behave like small towns, and a single brand voice copy-pasted everywhere pleases no one. We build programs that know which Charlotte they are talking to &mdash; the strategy, content and paid work is all on our <a href=\"/services/\">services page</a> &mdash; and we would rather be interesting in two rooms than present in seven.</p>"),
